    <briefdescription>
<para>W3C <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage" kindref="compound">Baggage</ref> – arbitrary key/value pairs propagated with every span. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage" kindref="compound">Baggage</ref> items are thread-local by default; call <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage_1a0a27a84f572b5f1034a70386d6e7df04" kindref="member">Baggage::set()</ref> / <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage_1ae36e400b0d19c1764d2723067fe3cae0" kindref="member">Baggage::get()</ref> to access the current thread&apos;s baggage store.</para>
<para>The serialised form follows the W3C <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage" kindref="compound">Baggage</ref> header specification: key=value[,key=value]*</para>
<para>Usage: <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage_1a0a27a84f572b5f1034a70386d6e7df04" kindref="member">Baggage::set</ref>(&quot;tenant-id&quot;, &quot;acme&quot;); std::string tid = <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage_1ae36e400b0d19c1764d2723067fe3cae0" kindref="member">Baggage::get</ref>(&quot;tenant-id&quot;); auto headers = <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_baggage_1aa912d40c665050fcf02f155ae0b32169" kindref="member">Baggage::inject()</ref>; // {&quot;baggage&quot;: &quot;tenant-id=acme&quot;} Baggage::extract(incomingHeaders); // populate from inbound request </para>
    </detaileddescription>
